/**
 * @defgroup ShldGeo ShldGeo — Beam Shielding Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR beam-tunnel shielding (SHLD)
 *
 * @details
 * ShldGeo (module name SHLDGEO) models the beam-shielding walls placed
 * symmetrically at z = ±1750 cm in the east and west RHIC beam tunnels, and a
 * concrete floor section at z = ±2800 cm.  The shielding attenuates
 * secondary particles from the tunnel from entering the Wide Angle Hall.
 *
 * Each shield assembly (SHLX mother volume, BOX 170×150×100 cm) contains:
 * - Two concrete base pedestals (SHBS, 60×30×100 cm half-dimensions)
 *   supporting the structure from the tunnel floor.
 * - A concrete lateral slab (SHLS, 170×30×30 cm half-dims) spanning the
 *   full width.
 * - A back iron plate (SHBI) filling the remainder of the slab height.
 * - A forward iron plate (SHFI, half-thickness 47 cm, half-height 55 cm)
 *   with a rectangular beam-pipe aperture hole (SHOL, 20×10 cm half-dims).
 *
 * A separate concrete floor volume (SFLR, 3900×340×70 cm full dimensions)
 * is placed at z = ±2800 cm.
 *
 * Both the shield assemblies and the floor are placed in CAVE: the west
 * (−z) shield is rotated 180° about z so that the forward-iron face points
 * toward the interaction point.
 *
 * There is a single geometry configuration (version 1); the module is enabled
 * via the SHLDon setup and disabled via SHLDof.
 *
 * ## Setup configurations
 *
 * | Setup name | onoff | Description |
 * |------------|-------|-------------|
 * | SHLDof     | off   | Shielding disabled |
 * | SHLDon     | on    | Default beam-tunnel shielding |
 *
 * ## Volume hierarchy
 * @code
 * SHLX  (BOX Air — mother, placed ±1750 cm in CAVE)
 * ├── SHBS ×2  (BOX Concrete — base pedestals)
 * ├── SHLS     (BOX Concrete — lateral slab)
 * ├── SHBI     (BOX Iron — back iron plate)
 * └── SHFI     (BOX Iron — forward iron plate)
 *     └── SHOL (BOX Air — beam aperture hole)
 * SFLR  (BOX Concrete — tunnel floor, placed ±2800 cm in CAVE)
 * @endcode
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @file ShldGeo.xml
 * @brief STAR beam-tunnel shielding geometry (SHLDGEO module).
 * Single configuration (SHLG version 1).  Shield walls at z = ±1750 cm;
 * concrete floor at z = ±2800 cm.  Beam aperture hole 20×10 cm.
 * Author: Maxim Potekhin (15 August 2005).
 */

/**
 * @file ShldConfig.xml
 * @brief Setup registry for the STAR shielding (SHLD).
 * Defines SHLDof (disabled) and SHLDon (default shielding enabled).
 */

